<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Hungary (1920-1946)</h1><p class="st-meta">1920 CE – 1946 CE · capital Budapest</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Interwar Hungarian kingdom without a king, ruled by Regent Miklós Horthy, which sought to undo the Treaty of Trianon and was drawn into the Second World War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hungarian-soviet-republic">Hungarian Soviet Republic</a>, a national assembly restored the monarchy in 1920 but, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> barred, elected Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miklos-horthy">Miklós Horthy</a> regent on 1 March. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-trianon">Treaty of Trianon</a> in June 1920 took two-thirds of the former <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hungary-1867-1918">Kingdom of Hungary</a> (1867-1918). Former king Charles IV twice tried to return in 1921 and failed.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istvan-bethlen">István Bethlen</a> stabilised the conservative regime in the 1920s, with restricted voting and dominance of landowners. Revision of Trianon was the central aim, and through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna-awards">Vienna Awards</a> of 1938 and 1940 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> regained southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a> and northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-transylvania">Transylvania</a> with German and Italian support. Antisemitic laws began with the numerus clausus of 1920 and tightened from 1938.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> joined the war against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in 1941. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> occupied it in March 1944, and around 437,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> were deported, most to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auschwitz-concentration-camp">Auschwitz</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miklos-horthy">Horthy</a>'s attempt to leave the war in October 1944 led to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferenc-szalasi">Ferenc Szálasi's</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/government-of-national-unity">Government of National Unity</a>. The monarchy was abolished in February 1946.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-hungary-1920-1946.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Hungary (1920-1946)" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hungary_(1915-1918;_angels).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1920 CE – 1946 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Budapest</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Miklós Horthy, István Bethlen, Pál Teleki</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic and Protestant Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hungarian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Regency of Hungary, Horthy's Hungary</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1933&amp;focus=kingdom-of-hungary-1920-1946" aria-label="Kingdom of Hungary (1920-1946) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5125 512 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Hungary (1920-1946) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5445 768L5445 768M5445 768L5300 622M5445 768L5445 768M5445 768L5379 775M5445 768L5431 812M5445 768L5445 768M5445 768L5542 748"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5445 768h0M5300 622h0M5445 768h0M5379 775h0M5431 812h0M5445 768h0M5542 748h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5445 768h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5445 768h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Budapest. <a href="/atlas?year=1933&amp;focus=kingdom-of-hungary-1920-1946">On the atlas &rarr;</a><